    answer: '<p>It depends on your usage. Cloud hosting can be <strong>cheaper for variable traffic</strong> because you only pay for what you use. However, for consistent, predictable traffic, traditional hosting\'s fixed pricing might be more economical. Most small blogs spend $5-20/month on traditional hosting; cloud hosting for similar traffic might cost $10-50/month depending on the provider.</p>'
  },
  {
